\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{From a slice to a space of states}
\date{2026-11-27}

\p{The [normal transfer](fdip-01BF) acts on projected field
values from neighboring layers. A space of many-fermion states
would require an inner product on observables and a positive
transfer representing the Grassmann expectations. In Lüscher's
Wilson construction the hopping bound, gauge constraint and
fermionic boundary conditions enter the construction, as in
\ref{fdip-0087}. The distinction between positivity of a
determinant and reflection positivity of the full Grassmann
weight is described in \ref{fdip-00JB}. What additional
boundary and observable data would give this slice recurrence
such a representation?}
